+### Analysis of positive (non-zero) abundances {#sec-daa-pos}
+
+It may sometimes be biologically relevant to analyze only the positive
+(non-zero) relative abundances of taxa. We thus briefly show here how to
+perform such analysis using the `maaslin3()` function. Purely for
+illustration purposes, we show here the analysis with an interaction term.
+
+We proceed as in the previous sections. The difference
+compared to DPA (@sec-dpa-cov) is that we now have to
+extract `fit_data_abundance` (and not
+`fit_data_prevalence`) from the list object returned by `maaslin3()`. We also
+need to set `median_comparison_abundance = FALSE` in the function call as we
+want to estimate the differences of (positive) relative abundances and not make
+any compositional adjustments.
 
